+# Bug Assessment: Product review privacy, validation, authorization, and rating totals
+
+- **Slug**: ticket
+- **Created**: 2026-11-18T21:35:00+00:00
+- **Source**: pasted text
+- **Verdict**: valid
+- **Severity**: high
+
+## Report (verbatim or summarized)
+
+The ticket reports that public product reviews expose customer email and address data; repeat reviews and rating 9 produce server errors; merchant edits/deletions do not recalculate product ratings; and specifies the required response fields, validation, authorization, conflict/not-found statuses, and rating semantics.
+
+## Symptom
+
+Product review endpoints currently serialize a full readable customer object, accept or mishandle invalid ratings and customer identity, return 5xx for expected client conflicts, and maintain product rating totals incrementally without correcting edits or deletions. The expected behavior is a privacy-safe first-name-only public review, precise 400/403/404/409 responses, atomic refusal of invalid submissions, and an exact one-decimal half-up aggregate after every mutation.
+
+## Reproduction
+
+1. GET `/api/v1/product/{id}/reviews` for a product with a review and inspect the serialized customer object.
+2. POST `/api/v1/auth/products/{id}/reviews` as an authenticated customer with the supplied payload; repeat it for the same product, submit rating `9`, and submit another customer's `customerId`.
+3. PUT or DELETE `/api/v1/private/products/{id}/reviews/{reviewId}`, then GET `/api/v2/product/{sku}` and compare `rating` and `ratingCount` with the remaining reviews.
+
+## Suspected Code Paths
+
+- `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/store/api/v1/product/ProductReviewApi.java:48-100` — duplicate reviews are sent as 500, ratings above 5 as 503, and the request customer identity is not checked against the authenticated customer.
+- `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/store/api/v1/product/ProductReviewApi.java:141-239` — update/delete handling uses the wrong update ownership check, does not consistently validate product ownership, and maps expected failures through 5xx responses.
+- `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/populator/catalog/ReadableProductReviewPopulator.java:25-34` and `sm-shop-model/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/model/catalog/product/ReadableProductReview.java:8-20` — public review responses include a `ReadableCustomer`, whose population can expose fields beyond first name.
+- `sm-core/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/core/business/services/catalog/product/review/ProductReviewServiceImpl.java:58-107` — every save adds a new rating to cached totals, including updates, and no delete recalculation is performed.
+- `sm-core/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/core/business/repositories/catalog/product/review/ProductReviewRepository.java:19-29` — existing product/customer lookup can support duplicate detection, while product-scoped review lookup is needed for safe merchant mutations.
+- `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/mapper/catalog/ReadableMinimalProductMapper.java:80-92` — v2 product output consumes the persisted review average and count.
+
+## Root Cause Hypothesis
+
+Confidence: high. The review API contains explicit incorrect status codes and duplicated route declarations, does not derive/verify the authenticated customer, and uses `Double` range annotations that do not enforce whole-number input. The service treats update as create and has no delete aggregate path, while the public DTO embeds a broad customer DTO. These code paths directly explain all reported symptoms.
+
+## Proposed Remediation
+
+**Preferred**: Make the public review DTO contain only id, rating, description, date, and a nested reviewer object exposing only first name (or a dedicated minimal reviewer field). Enforce integer ratings from 1 through 5 before persistence, use the authenticated principal/customer for authorization, return 403 for mismatched customer ids and 409 for duplicates, and ensure rejected requests return before any save. Scope merchant PUT/DELETE by both product id and review id and return 404 when absent or mismatched.
+
+Centralize review aggregate recalculation in the product-review service: after create, update, and delete, load the current reviews, compute count and a `BigDecimal` average rounded to one decimal with `RoundingMode.HALF_UP`, and persist zero values when none remain. Ensure update replaces the existing review rather than incrementing totals and delete invokes the same recalculation.
+
+**Files likely to change**:
+- `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/store/api/v1/product/ProductReviewApi.java`
+- `sm-shop-model/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/model/catalog/product/ReadableProductReview.java`
+- `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/populator/catalog/ReadableProductReviewPopulator.java`
+- `sm-core/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/core/business/services/catalog/product/review/ProductReviewService.java`
+- `sm-core/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/core/business/services/catalog/product/review/ProductReviewServiceImpl.java`
+- `sm-core/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/core/business/repositories/catalog/product/review/ProductReviewRepository.java`
+- relevant review API/service tests under `sm-shop/src/test` and `sm-core/src/test`
+
+**Tests to add or update**:
+- Public review JSON contains only the allowed review fields and reviewer first name, with no email or address.
+- Create rejects ratings 0, 6, 9, fractional values, and mismatched customer ids with 400/403 and leaves the repository unchanged.
+- Duplicate create returns 409 and leaves one review.
+- Merchant update/delete return 404 for missing or wrong-product review ids and recalculate average/count for normal and empty-product cases.
+- Aggregate calculation rounds one decimal half-up after create, update, and delete, and v2 product mapping exposes the values.
+
+## Risks & Considerations
+
+- Removing customer fields from the public review contract is an intentional API privacy tightening; merchant/private response compatibility should be checked separately.
+- Authentication principal-to-customer resolution must use the existing store/security conventions and must not trust the request body customer id.
+- Recomputing aggregates reads all reviews per mutation; correctness is preferred, but a database aggregate query may be needed if review volume is large.
+- Existing persisted averages may be stale; the mutation path will correct them, while a migration/backfill could be considered separately.
+
+## Open Questions
+
+- None blocking the requested implementation.
